      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "If $\\frac{{w}^{2}}{4}+22=0,$ then $w=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{w}^{2}}{4}+22 & =0 \\\\ \\frac{{w}^{2}}{4} & =-22 \\\\ {w}^{2} & =-88\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy taking square root, we obtain:\n\n$$\nw=\\pm \\sqrt{-88}\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $w$ using the imaginary unit $\\text{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w & =\\pm \\sqrt{-88} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{88\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{88}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm 2\\sqrt{22}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm 2\\sqrt{22}\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
